        "title": "BELKAHVE Construction, Metal Recycling, Trade and Industry Inc.",
        "image": null,
        "alt": "Image from BELKAHVE Construction, Metal Recycling, Trade and Industry Inc.",
        "lead": "TURNING WASTE INTO RESOURCES, AND RESOURCES INTO THE FUTURE",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "In line with our sustainability vision, we established Belkahve Inc., a municipal subsidiary, to help return waste to the economy and strengthen the circular economy. Waste management begins where waste is generated. Under a defined collection programme, we collect waste separated by type from producers' premises and transport it in suitable vehicles to licensed facilities. At the facility, we weigh, inspect and record the waste. This allows us to track where the waste came from, how much there is and which process it is sent to."
              }
            ],
            "align": "justify"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "We return the recyclable portion of waste separated at the facility to the economy. The portion that cannot be recovered as material but is suitable for energy production is prepared through processes such as shredding and sizing. At licensed energy recovery facilities, this waste can be used to produce heat, steam or electricity, depending on the facility's technical infrastructure."
              }
            ],
            "align": "justify"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "Through this system, we aim to reduce the amount of waste sent to landfill and use resources more efficiently. Collection and weighing records also help us plan routes and transport processes more efficiently. Activities such as collection, sorting, facility operation and maintenance create opportunities for local employment and economic activity."
              }
            ],
            "align": "justify"
          }
        ],
        "metrics": [],
        "galleryKeys": [
          "belkahve"
        ],
        "leadAlign": "justify"
